@@s001 Homework: how to pass them
@@s002 <span>Exam</span><span>admission</span>
@@s003 Homework: how to pass them
@@s004 To be admitted to the exam you must pass <b>5 homework out of 10</b>. A homework passes if it <b>compiles</b> and fails very few tests. Here: rules, deadlines, and how to read the test output to understand what to fix.
@@s005 The rules
@@s006 How many
@@s007 about 13 exercise sets, <b>10 assessed</b>, <b>5 passed</b> are needed
@@s008 First assessed
@@s009 week 3 (Option), submitted in week 4
@@s010 Who
@@s011 individual: you may discuss, but you write the code yourself
@@s012 What you submit
@@s013 only <code>Exercises.scala</code>, no zip
@@s014 Deadline
@@s015 <b>Tuesday 10:00</b>, one week after the lecture
@@s016 Resubmission
@@s017 if it does not pass or you miss the deadline: by <b>Sunday 23:59</b>, two weeks after the deadline
@@s018 When it passes
@@s019 1) The code <b>compiles</b>. 2) It fails <b>at most 5</b> tests.
@@s020 Two different numbers
@@s021 The week 1 slides say "at most 5 tests can fail". The LearnIT page of the course says "only six or less tests fail". Stick to the stricter rule (5) and, if you are at the limit, ask on the Discord.
